September 10, 1994

Included in this directory is an Autocall.GPF with some scripts included that I'm
using on my BBS to get around Trapdoor and my USRobotics modem. 
 _It is far from a perfect_  solution, but it works for me.

Change the path at the top of the file as necessary, and replace the Autocall.GPF
file in the Fax-IT/ directory with it.

Another route I was using for awhile was to have my system quit Trapdoor and
run GPFax several times during the day through my Cron program.  The entries
in your Cron_tab file would look much the same as the first couple of lines of 
Autofax.GPF and the additions to the Quit: statement in it.

With any luck, GPFax will support OwnDevUnit.library and support Class 2.0 FAX in
its next release which will help it live alot more peaceably with Trapdoor and
USR modems.

I realize that this is a difficult installation to accomplish.
If you're having trouble getting set up, drop me a line at one of the places listed
in the Cnet docs and I'll see if I can't help you out.

-Malcolm Anderson
